30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data shows a huge imbalance. Two people use the room far more than the rest, and cleaning is unfairly distributed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It's worse than we thought. Our only unplanned talks are by the printer, and awkward conversations happen in front of everyone.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Most of us spend twenty-five minutes just getting a hot lunch. Plus, we're eating at our desks, leaving crumbs everywhere.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We spent 68,000 yen last year on tiny external rentals. A meeting fit-out is 141,000, while a kitchen is 96,000.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The wall is just plasterboard; everything is audible. However, the store room has had zero facilities issues.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, if we are paying for external rooms for small groups, a dedicated internal space seems logical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, if the walls are that thin, a kitchen or a loud meeting room might be disruptive to those sitting nearby.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"But if we have a kitchen, we stop the desk-crumbs and the long walks for food. That saves hours of productivity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,The external hire is a recurring drain. Investing in a fit-out now saves us money in the long run.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,I worry about the noise. A kitchen or a meeting room could become a source of constant distraction.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A meeting space with a calendar would solve the ""first-come"" conflict and the unfair usage patterns.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"We desperately need a place for private, difficult conversations. A quiet room or a meeting space provides that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, a calendar is fine, but it doesn't solve the hunger or the mess at the desks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A kitchen is cheaper to install, but a meeting space eliminates the external invoices entirely.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"If we choose a quiet room, we preserve the peace of the office and stop the noise leakage.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We must balance the need for structure with the actual needs of the staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,The social fabric of this office is fraying. We need a space that fosters connection or privacy.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I still think the time wasted on lunch is the biggest hidden cost here.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's look at the options. We need a professional solution that stops the financial leak.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us consider which option brings the most harmony to the environment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C, the Meeting Space, provides the most structure. A shared calendar removes all ambiguity.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C also allows for those necessary private conversations that we currently lack.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,I strongly prefer Option A. An Open Kitchen solves the lunch commute and the desk cleanliness issue.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is the most rational. It stops the 68,000 yen annual loss and provides a professional utility.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B, the Quiet Room, is the only one that guarantees the peace of those sitting by the door.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the kitchen doesn't solve the usage conflict; it might actually increase the mess.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, a quiet room is peaceful, but it doesn't help us resolve the interpersonal tensions we have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, the mess is already here at our desks! A kitchen centralizes it.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,The cost-benefit analysis heavily favors the Meeting Space. It's a one-time investment to stop a recurring cost.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Harmony is not just about costs, Shunichi. It is about the quality of the air and sound we breathe.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot support a kitchen if it means more unplanned chaos. I vote for the Meeting Space.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Ryuji. We need a place to actually talk. I vote for the Meeting Space.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I can't ignore the twenty-five-minute walk. I'm sticking with the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,The numbers are clear. I vote for the Meeting Space.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,I still believe in the value of silence. I vote for the Quiet Room.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
